{
  "id": "Compound::DB00252 - Gene::100861540",
  "verbalization": "Phenytoin is associated with Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p through a network of interactions involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Phenytoin, as an inducer of multiple CYP450 enzymes, may influence the expression or activity of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p. Specifically, Phenytoin is classified as an inducer of CYP3A enzymes, including CYP3A4 and CYP3A5, which are known to bind to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p. This indicates a potential regulatory mechanism where Phenytoin could modulate the expression of these genes, thereby affecting the activity of the CYP3A7-cyp3a51p complex. The shared lowest common ancestor with other compounds like Carbamazepine and Ritonavir further supports a common pathway in which Phenytoin influences the expression of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p through the induction of CYP450 enzymes. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving enzyme induction and gene regulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
